Lions Name Outstanding Young Men
Bill Latham, senior at El Paso High School, and Juan Salvador, Jefferson High senior, 
have been selected as “Student Lions of the Month” by tke El Paso Lions Club.
This award is given to boys who have been outstanding in school, church, and social activities and have been both a good student and a good
citizen.
Bill is a member of Senior National Honor Society, Language Honor Society, Slide Rule
Club, and Masque and Gavel Club.
A football and track letterman, Bill is working as a student assistant in charge of Girls Poetry in the up-coming
El Paso High School debate tournament.
Juan is president of the Jefferson National Honor Society
and is an All-District baseball player. He is a member of the
Number Sense Club, which is an organization that works with
numbers for speed and accuracy.
Juan, who plans to attend college and major in mathematics, said, ‘““Through this award,
I have gotten to meet many interesting people.” He listed Judge Sam Blackham, Andy
Cohen, and John Phelan as some of those he has met.

El_Paso_Times_1966_01_28_24.jpg Picture with New Officers of El Paso Sports Association with article 
